<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Conquest for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45624/emblem-of-conquest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></a> is the new raid currency introduced in Phase 2, this is obtainable through 10 and 25-man Ulduar, as well as the daily heroic dungeon quest from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=20735/archmage-landalock">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Archmage Lan'dalock</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>All gear from the conquest vendor is iLevel-232 and because of that is likely to be an upgrade in one way or another for most players, we're only providing one way to approach your emblem gear though consider that some of these upgrades can be situationally very strong and might be just the item you're looking for.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46173/conquerors-aegis-breastplate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Breastplate</span></a> is a lucrative initial pick up, it sits as one of the best chests in phase 2, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46175/conquerors-aegis-faceguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_97.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Faceguard</span></a> also being a contender for the BiS head slot lets you capitalize on guaranteeing your 2-set bonus as well as having some of the best items for these slots.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45834/gauntlets-of-the-royal-watch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of the Royal Watch</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45821/shard-of-the-crystal-forest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_47.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shard of the Crystal Forest</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45825/shieldwarder-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_48a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shieldwarder Girdle</span></a> are optional pieces but being cheaper you are investing less emblems for a higher return on iLevel than if you were to buy an expensive tier piece ahead of these. Well itemized for hit, these will also assist you in capping out early and are hard to replace for that purpose.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45087/runed-orb">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_runedorb_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Orb</span></a> is a definitive consideration if you know that your guild is not giving you early dibs on your orbs, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45560/spiked-deathdealers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spiked Deathdealers</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45551/indestructible-plate-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_45a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indestructible Plate Girdle</span></a> are both powerful BoE crafts that likewise contend for BiS in their respective slots.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45842/wyrmguard-legplates">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wyrmguard Legplates</span></a> is not really a worthwhile pick-up, the primary use of these legs are for solo tanking the adds on heroic <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_anubarak.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
