<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="hands">Hands for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45487/handguards-of-revitalization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Handguards of Revitalization</span></a> are significantly better statted than any of the other gloves, though most of that is afforded through its major leap in iLevel, the stat spread itself is not extraordinary and in this case, the addition of an extra gem slot makes this weaker than it otherwise would be. Despite all that, it's got a fairly huge leg up on its competitors in <i>tankyness</i>.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45834/gauntlets-of-the-royal-watch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of the Royal Watch</span></a> is a well balanced set of gloves with a very efficient budget, it doesn't waste any of it on parry or otherwise expensive stats. The hit might be overkill for some though there are no real alternative gloves if you aren't doing hardmode. However perhaps best of all is that it's purchaseable for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45624/emblem-of-conquest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></a>, meaning there is no competition or unnecessary waiting for these.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46174/conquerors-aegis-handguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Handguards</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45383/valorous-aegis-handguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valorous Aegis Handguards</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45228/handguards-of-the-enclave">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_67.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Handguards of the Enclave</span></a> are all leaning a bit too heavily into their SBV to pick them up and while there's nothing wrong with block value in phase 2, there's just too much magic damage to rely on this situational mitigation.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45310/gauntlets-of-the-iron-furnace">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_54.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of the Iron Furnace</span></a> is just a weird item, you might pick these up if you don't have anything else, they compete with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40580/valorous-redemption-handguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valorous Redemption Handguards</span></a> but both of them are obsolete by the time you step your foot into Ulduar.<br/>
<br/>We don't recommend that you pick <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44488/enchant-gloves-precision">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_greaterheal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Gloves - Precision</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44484/enchant-gloves-expertise">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Gloves - Expertise</span></a> as an offensive glove enchant, it's almost always better to go with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44625/enchant-gloves-armsman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Gloves - Armsman</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Glove Enchant</b> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=63770/reticulated-armor-webbing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reticulated Armor Webbing</span></a> &gt; <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44625/enchant-gloves-armsman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Gloves - Armsman</span></a>. If you have <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=164/blacksmithing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_blacksmithing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blacksmithing</span></a> you can also attach <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_61.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a> to your gloves.<div class="pad"></div>
