<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="waist">Waist for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45551/indestructible-plate-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_45a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indestructible Plate Girdle</span></a> sits unique in the belt slot for phase 2 as the only belt with a focus on high meaningful avoidance, compared to the alternatives this is the tankiest option. While worse in threat and DPS than most other counterparts on this list it does have high strength from which it draws considerable offensive power from. Being a crafted BoE makes this highly accessible and may lighten the load on your raid, and provide you with a solid guaranteed item<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45825/shieldwarder-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_48a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shieldwarder Girdle</span></a> is the clear tanking belt for when you need to hit cap, it's a straight linear upgrade from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45304/stormtempered-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_49b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormtempered Girdle</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45241/belt-of-colossal-rage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_49c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Colossal Rage</span></a> is a DPS belt, we try and avoid taking gear like this though it's warranted a mention since it being a 252 iLevel item, has an above the norm item budget, putting this on par or ahead in EHP with actual tanking belts.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45139/dragonslayers-brace">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_34.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonslayer's Brace</span></a> is a consolation prize if you never get any of the above belts, though seeing how accessible they are you'll likely never use this in Phase 2. However keep this in your bank, it may be relevant to you in phase 3.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41611/eternal-belt-buckle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_36.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Belt Buckle</span></a> is a universal item enhancement for your belt. Those with <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> also get access to a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54793/frag-belt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frag Belt</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
