<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="legs">Legs for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45594/legplates-of-the-endless-void">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legplates of the Endless Void</span></a> unsurprisingly sits as the highest value legs that you can acquire in phase 2. Besides the huge iLevel upgrade over the alternatives the additional socket and emphasis on high value avoidance put these ahead.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46176/conquerors-aegis-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_24.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Legguards</span></a> is advantageous over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45267/saronite-plated-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Saronite Plated Legguards</span></a>, while the latter have similar EHP to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45594/legplates-of-the-endless-void">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legplates of the Endless Void</span></a> the tier legs gives you additional access to the set bonus, as well as an overall more balanced item.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45295/gilded-steel-legplates">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gilded Steel Legplates</span></a> are very advantageous in that they come from 10-man and give a solid middle ground between first and second best options in this slot. In some respects this is even better than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46176/conquerors-aegis-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_24.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Legguards</span></a> assuming you don't get 2 or 4-piece set bonus through your legs.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Leg Armor:</b> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=38373/frosthide-leg-armor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frosthide Leg Armor</span></a> otherwise if you have <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> you can make <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60583/jormungar-leg-reinforcements">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jormungar Leg Reinforcements</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
