<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 2</h3>Not much changes in phase 2. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46021/royal-seal-of-king-llane">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Seal of King Llane</span></a> are practically linear upgrades from phase 1 and what was strong then is still functional now. Generally you pick and choose trinkets based on the occasion, every trinket has extraordinary use when applied correctly. If you're unsure, stamina &amp; armor trinkets are very strong.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45313/furnace-stone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Furnace Stone</span></a> is perhaps the most interesting, with a weak passive but potentially wicked on-use this is very similar to the beloved <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=32501/shadowmoon-insignia">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowsongamethyst_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowmoon Insignia</span></a> from TBC in both form and function against physical attacks.<div class="pad"></div>
